        "mode": "html",
        "content": "<div style=\"padding:14px 18px;background:linear-gradient(90deg,#0b1020 0%,#20357a 38%,#8e2b2b 68%,#f6b73c 100%);border-radius:12px;color:#fff;font-family:system-ui,sans-serif\"><div style=\"display:flex;align-items:center;gap:14px\"><div style=\"font-size:34px;line-height:1\">🏔️</div><div><div style=\"font-size:21px;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:.3px\">Cloud Yatra · Live Observatory</div><div style=\"opacity:.92;font-size:12.5px;margin-top:3px\">Every panel below is real traffic from a little platformer about a Nepali traveller climbing from the jungle to the Himalaya. Play the game above — then watch these numbers move.</div></div></div><div style=\"margin-top:10px;font-size:11.5px;opacity:.85;line-height:1.5\">How to read it: <b>At a glance</b> is the headline. <b>The climb</b> shows how far players get (a classic funnel). <b>Yatri's journey</b> breaks down what happens on the trail. <b>Scores</b> is the shared leaderboard, <b>Around the world</b> maps where people play, and <b>Chaos Mode</b> is where I break my own backend on purpose to watch it recover.</div></div>"
